{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","statement":"Additions made since the React 19 RC was shared in April 2024 include pre-warming for suspended trees and new React DOM static APIs.","source_span":"**Pre-warming for suspended trees**... **React DOM static APIs**"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","fact_refs":[0],"question":"When did React 19 become available as a stable release on npm?","answer":"December 5, 2024."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","fact_refs":[1,2],"question":"What is useActionState in React 19, and what was it previously called?","answer":"useActionState is a new React 19 hook for handling common Action use cases; it was previously called ReactDOM.useFormState in Canary releases, and useFormState has since been deprecated."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","fact_refs":[3],"question":"What are \"Actions\" in React 19?","answer":"Actions are, by convention, functions that use async transitions in React 19; they automatically manage pending state, optimistic updates, error handling, and forms."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Which new React 19 hook is used to manage optimistic updates?","answer":"useOptimistic."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What new capability do <form> elements gain in React 19?","answer":"They can accept functions passed to the action and formAction props, which use Actions by default and automatically reset the form after submission."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19","fact_refs":[7],"question":"What two features were added to React 19 since the RC was shared in April 2024?","answer":"Pre-warming for suspended trees and new React DOM static APIs."}
